# =============================================================================
# WHAT IS COMMITTED EVIDENCE VS WHAT IS REGENERABLE
# =============================================================================
# COMMITTED (small, citable, and the thing a reader verifies against):
#   results/all_runs.csv            one row per (scenario, model, seed)
#   results/federated_all_runs.csv  one row per (arm, seed)
#   results/manifest.json           git SHA, config, library versions, real step
#                                   counts, solved widths, CSV hashes
#   results/claims.json             machine-readable claims with provenance
#   results/tables/*.csv            everything the report cites
#   results/figures/*.png           everything the report shows
#   RESULTS.md                      generated from the above, CI-diff-checked
#
# IGNORED (large, regenerable, or not evidence):
#   results/raw/                    per-run logs
#   results/checkpoints/            weights -- the manifest is the anchor, not .pt
#   anything under a scratch or smoke output directory
#
# The previous version of this repository committed 1,031 generated files
# totalling 85.3% of its bytes, including 127 files from runs its own README
# described as throwaway smoke tests.
# =============================================================================

# --- regenerable run artifacts ---
results/raw/
results/checkpoints/
results_smoke/
results_quick/
results_fed_smoke/
results_*_smoke/
checkpoints/
checkpoints_*/
logs/
logs_*/
plots/
tensorboard/
*.log

# --- model weights: never committed; manifest.json is the reproducibility anchor ---
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt

# --- python ---
